Company: Visory Health
Title: Quality Assurance Lead
Salary Min:
Salary Max:
Description:
About the job

About the Company


Visory Health is growing! Come work for an industry leader in the health technology field. At Visory Health, we apply our unique & in-depth healthcare knowledge to create healthcare access for retail pharmacies, physicians, and consumers. We are looking for a QA Lead to support members of our team in completion of technology projects that uphold our business initiatives.


Visory Health is leading the market shift to cash in healthcare by developing proprietary technology, analytics, and consumer engagement platforms that allow consumers to access lower cost prescription medicines. We’re doing healthcare differently. At Visory Health, we believe that no one, especially women, families, caregivers, and underserved communities should have to go without lifesaving medication. Our healthcare system is complicated, and we want to cut through that noise by bringing better prescription prices to everyone. That’s why we developed the Visory Health Prescription Savings Card. We’re women-owned, women-led, and we’re just getting started!



About the Role


This role is ideal for someone who can manage QA team members while also driving high-level testing strategy, process improvements, and quality standards across the organization. Although this role is primarily remote, some in-office training and occasional visits to our St. Louis office may be required.



Responsibilities


    Manage the QA team, including assisting with prioritization and allocation of QA resources
    Establish and enforce QA standards, best practices, and expectations across the team
    Work with the development team to develop, publish, and update the project plan.
    Track issues found while testing and collaborate with the development team on how to resolve.
    Communicate directly with stakeholders on issues found and their impacts to a planned deployment.
    Perform high-level, exploratory, and end-to-end testing on complex or critical features
    Validate automation workflows across systems
    Identify testing gaps and quality risks that may not be covered by standard test cases



Qualifications


    3+ years of experience in Quality Assurance
    Proven experience managing or leading QA teams
    Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, including the ability to speak with all levels of employees, vendors and team members
    Flexible, as priorities can change quickly, day-to-day and even hour-to-hour
    Keen attention to detail and efficient problem-solving skills
    Knowledge of CI/CD practices
    Experience creating and executing detailed and complex manual and automation testing scenarios.
    Solid understanding of system integrations, data validation testing, and UAT coordination
    Previous experience working with Jira, Azure DevOps, or similar tools



Required Skills


    Healthcare/Health Technology experience
    Previous experience working with database testing and post SQL
    Previous experience with Detox, Playwrite, Selenium, and/or Appium.
    Previous experience with Typescript, ReAct Native and/or Javascript.



Visory Health is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. If you have any questions about this, please contact us.



Awards


    Inc. 5000 2023, 2022, 2021. Awarded to the fastest growing private companies in America.
    St. Louis Business Journal Best Places to Work 2023
    Top 50 Inspiring Workplaces (awarded by NOAM) 2022
    Inc. Magazine Best Places to Work 2022

Featured benefits

Medical insurance, Vision insurance, Dental insurance, 401(k)

