Description:

As a System Integration Test Architect, you will manage system test architecture, validate integrations, oversee backlog management, and lead cross-team alignment for testing processes.
Summary Generated by Built In
Career Area:
Technology, Digital and Data
Job Description:
Your Work Shapes the World at Caterpillar Inc.
When you join Caterpillar, you're joining a global team who cares not just about the work we do - but also about each other. We are the makers, problem solvers, and future world builders who are creating stronger, more sustainable communities. We don't just talk about progress and innovation here - we make it happen, with our customers, where we work and live. Together, we are building a better world, so we can all enjoy living in it.
Role Definition
As a System Integration Test Architect, you will drive end-to-end validation across complex, multi-program ecosystems and to deliver solutions that improve quality and enable testing. This role sits at the intersection of product, engineering, and quality, ensuring that system integrations are well-defined, gaps are identified early, and validation is executed in alignment with system test strategies.
What you will do:

    Act as a technical product owner for system test architecture scope, aligning with business and engineering goals
    Own and manage backlog, including prioritization, refinement, and delivery tracking
    Define requirements for new solutions that improve quality, efficiency, and enable testing
    Drive integration validation across multiple programs and systems
    Identify integration gaps, risks, and dependencies across systems, data flows, and environments
    Ensure test teams execute validation in accordance with defined system test strategies
    Lead cross-team alignment between engineering, QA, product, and program stakeholders
    Monitor and report on validation progress and coverage
    Continuously improve integration testing processes, tooling, and coverage


What you will have:

    Effective Communications: Understanding of effective communication concepts, tools and techniques; ability to effectively transmit, receive, and accurately interpret ideas, information, and needs through the application of appropriate communication behaviors.
    Requirements Analysis: Knowledge of tools, methods, and techniques of requirement analysis; ability to elicit, analyze and record required business functionality and non-functionality requirements to ensure the success of a system or software development project.
    Application Design, Architecture: Knowledge of basic activities and deliverables of application design; ability to utilize application design methodologies, tools and techniques to convert business requirements and logical models into a test strategies.
    Software Product Testing: Knowledge of software product testing; ability to design, plan, and execute testing strategies and tactics to ensure software product quality and adherence to stated requirements. 


Top candidates will have:

    Typically have 12 years or more of software engineering experience
    Experience as a Technical Product Owner, System Integration Lead, or QA/Test Lead in complex systems
    Strong technical understanding of APIs and system integrations
    Experience owning and managing product backlog in Agile environment
    Ability to read and interpret API specs, logs, and integration data flows
    Experience defining end-to-end test scenarios and system validation strategies
    Ability to identify testing and quality gaps across systems and translate them into actionable plans
    Experience working across multiple teams/programs with complex dependencies
    Experience with defect management and root cause analysis
    Hands-on SQL
    Experience with test automation
    Familiarity with event-driven architectures and microservices
    Experience building or working with data quality/validation platforms


Additional Details:

    This position has the option to be based out of either our Chicago, IL, Peoria, IL, or Irving, TX (Dallas) offices.
    Relocation assistance is NOT available for this position
    Visa sponsorship is NOT available with this position now or in the future. 


