URL: https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4414597572
Company: Ovidius AI B.V.
Title: Senior Quality Assurance Engineer (US BASED)
Salary Min: 
Salary Max: 
Description:
About the job

THE ROLE 

We're looking for a Senior QA Engineer — someone who doesn't just run test cases but pressure-tests the entire surface area of AI-powered systems. You'll be the human signal in a stack that's largely built by AI, catching the failure modes that automated checks and LLM evals miss.


This role sits at the intersection of traditional QA discipline and applied AI: you'll design test strategies for agentic workflows, validate retrieval-augmented generation outputs, stress-test multi-step automation pipelines, and own the quality bar for systems where "it usually works" isn't good enough.

The ideal candidate has deep hands-on QA experience and pairs it with a working understanding of how modern AI systems actually break — non-deterministic outputs, prompt regressions, retrieval drift, tool-use failures, and the long tail of edge cases that only a curious human will surface.


We're starting fractional / contract because we want to find the right person before committing to full-time. Strong fit can convert.


REQUIRED SKILLS & EXPERTISE


AI System Testing Hands-on experience testing LLM-powered applications and agentic workflows:

    Designing test plans for non-deterministic systems
    Building and maintaining evaluation suites (golden sets, regression catalogs, prompt regressions)
    Identifying hallucination patterns, tool-use failures, and silent degradations
    Comfortable distinguishing between model issues, prompt issues, retrieval issues, and orchestration issues


Manual & Exploratory Testing 5+ years of structured QA work, with strong exploratory testing instincts. You can:

    Write clear, reproducible bug reports with minimal back-and-forth
    Design test cases from ambiguous requirements
    Build mental models of complex systems quickly and find the seams
    Prioritize defects by user impact, not just severity labels


Test Case Design & Documentation Strong command of:

    Gherkin / BDD-style scenarios when appropriate
    Edge case enumeration (boundary, null, malformed, adversarial inputs)
    Regression suites that stay maintainable as the product evolves
    Clean, searchable bug tickets in Linear, Jira, or similar


API & Database Testing Proficient with:

    Postman, Bruno, or similar for API contract testing
    Reading and writing SQL to verify data integrity (PostgreSQL / Supabase)
    Validating webhook payloads, event flows, and async pipelines
    Inspecting logs and traces to root-cause issues before filing tickets


Workflow & Automation QA Working experience testing automation platforms:

    n8n, Zapier, Make, or comparable workflow tools
    Validating conditional branches, error recovery, retry logic, and webhook integrations
    Verifying end-to-end behavior across third-party API integrations


Claude Cowork & Plugin Testing Familiarity with Claude Cowork (Anthropic's agentic desktop environment) as a power user:

    Testing custom Skills and Plugins for trigger accuracy and output quality
    Validating MCP connector behavior and scheduled task reliability
    Stress-testing agentic workflows that span multiple business tools



WHAT YOU'LL DO


    Own the QA function for our AI agent systems — from prompt-level evals to end-to-end user journeys
    Build and maintain regression suites for RAG pipelines, agent workflows, and n8n automations
    Run release validation on every shipped change — Skills, Plugins, agents, and platform updates
    Catch the failures AI can't catch itself: hallucinations, subtle context loss, tool-misuse, brittle prompts, retrieval drift
    Write reproducible bug reports that engineers can act on without a 20-message thread
    Partner with engineering to design testability into systems from day one
    Build a body of test cases, eval sets, and QA documentation that scales with the team
    Establish QA process and standards for an AI-first agency — what gets tested, when, and how
    Triage incoming bugs from clients and internal users, separating signal from noise



NICE TO HAVE


    Python or JavaScript — enough to write small scripts, parse logs, or extend test harnesses
    Playwright / Cypress — for the web app surface area, when it makes sense
    LLM evaluation tooling — Braintrust, Langfuse, Promptfoo, or similar
    Prompt engineering experience — you don't need to be a prompter, but you should understand why prompts fail
    Security testing exposure — prompt injection, jailbreak attempts, data leakage scenarios
    No-code / low-code QA — testing Webflow, Bubble, Airtable, or similar platforms
    Client-facing experience — comfortable reproducing issues alongside non-technical stakeholders
    ISTQB or similar certification — not required, but signals process discipline



TECH STACK YOU'LL TOUCH

Claude API · Claude Code · Managed Agents · Claude Cowork · RAG / pgvector · Supabase · PostgreSQL · SAP · n8n · MCP · Linear · Slack · Snowflake


ENGAGEMENT

    Type: Fractional / contract to start (10–25 hrs/week, flexible)
    Location: Remote — async-friendly
    Conversion: Strong fit can move to full-time
    Rate: Competitive, based on experience



If you're the kind of QA engineer who finds the bug nobody else thought to look for, who treats "it works on my machine" as a personal insult, and who's already curious about how AI systems silently fail in production — we want to hear from you.


PS. This role exists because our engineers ship fast with AI, but the only thing AI still can't reliably do is QA itself. That's where you come in.

--

