Company: CareMetx
Title: Senior QA Manager, Product Engineering
Salary Min: 
Salary Max: 
Description:
Description

From intake to outcomes, CareMetx is dedicated to delivering industry-leading patient access solutions and support services that help patients quickly start and stay on specialty therapy treatments. We provide scalable, efficient digital hub services for pharmaceutical companies and healthcare providers, streamlining workflows with seamless integration for patient enrollment, consent, and prior authorization. Our best-in-class patient support services enhance every step of care, connecting patients, providers, and brands to drive better outcomes and accelerate time-to-therapy.  


Job Title: Senior QA Manager, Product Engineering

POSITION SUMMARY:

CareMetx is seeking a highly experienced Senior QA Manager, Product Engineering to own and elevate end-to-end quality assurance across our product engineering organization. This is a senior leadership role critical to ensuring the quality, reliability, and scalability of our pharmaceutical hub services platform — including CRM systems, benefits verification services, integration platforms, and customer-facing applications that serve a significant number of patients and healthcare providers.

In this role, you will define and drive the overarching QA strategy across multiple product teams, lead and coordinate distributed testing teams (including offshore resources), and serve as a trusted quality partner to product owners, engineering leaders, and executive stakeholders. You will elevate QA from a functional discipline to a strategic organizational capability — embedding quality practices across the full software development lifecycle. This role focuses on integration testing and cross-team quality assurance, as individual engineering teams own their unit testing.

 PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:

 QA Strategy and Planning

    Define, own, and continuously evolve a comprehensive, multi-year QA strategy for end-to-end testing across our multi-system healthcare technology platform, including CRM applications, benefits verification services, integration layers, and customer-facing portals.
    Design and lead testing strategies for complex cross-team workflows involving multiple systems, ensuring thorough coverage of integration points and data flows.
    Establish quality metrics, KPIs, and executive-level reporting dashboards to provide full visibility into quality status across all products, teams, and initiatives.
    Set and enforce test documentation standards, templates, and best practices adopted across the organization.
    Define test coverage requirements for new features and platforms, ensuring an appropriate and defensible balance between manual and automated testing approaches.
    Proactively identify systemic quality risks across the portfolio and develop mitigation plans before they impact delivery or production.

Test Execution and Team Leadership

    Lead and scale end-to-end testing operations, including management of distributed and offshore QA resources across multiple time zones.
    Drive QA activities for major releases and strategic initiatives, coordinating testing efforts across multiple engineering teams to ensure delivery timelines and quality standards are met.
    Oversee test execution cycles including regression testing, integration testing, and user acceptance testing for complex healthcare workflows.
    Establish, monitor, and continuously improve service level agreements (SLAs) for defect resolution, holding engineering leaders accountable for timely and high-quality bug fixes.
    Champion a consistent, scalable approach to test planning and execution that can grow with the organization.

Collaboration and Stakeholder Management

    Serve as the senior quality voice in cross-functional discussions with product owners, engineering leaders, and executive management — translating quality risks into business impact.
    Lead and facilitate efficient bug triage sessions with engineering teams, driving clear prioritization and accountability for defect resolution.
    Partner with product management to define acceptance criteria and ensure features meet business requirements and regulatory standards before release.
    Collaborate with the architecture team and engineering leadership to ensure QA strategies are tightly aligned with architectural decisions and long-term technology roadmaps.
    Influence organizational decisions around tooling, process, and resourcing with data-backed quality insights.

Automation and Process Improvement

    Own and advance the organization's automation strategy, driving measurable reductions in manual testing effort while maintaining comprehensive coverage.
    Lead the design and implementation of automation frameworks targeting critical user workflows, integration scenarios, and regression coverage.
    Establish and mature CI/CD quality checkpoints and automated testing pipelines to prevent regressions from reaching production.
    Continuously evaluate and champion testing tools, frameworks, and approaches that improve testing efficiency and effectiveness across the organization.
    Foster a culture of quality throughout the engineering organization, promoting shift-left testing practices, engineering ownership of unit tests, and quality-first thinking at every stage of development.

Healthcare Domain and Compliance

    Ensure QA strategies fully account for healthcare industry regulations including HIPAA compliance, PHI data protection, and pharmaceutical industry requirements.
    Validate complex healthcare workflows including benefits verification, prior authorization, patient enrollment, and pharmacy integrations.
    Lead testing of integration scenarios with external healthcare systems, pharmaceutical CRMs (Veeva, Salesforce Health Cloud), and third-party vendors.
    Uphold and continuously strengthen quality standards for systems processing sensitive patient data and mission-critical healthcare transactions.
    Validate data accuracy and integrity across complex healthcare data flows spanning multiple systems and integration points.

Team Development and Organizational Growth

    Build, mentor, and develop QA team members, accelerating their technical growth and creating a high-performing, engaged quality organization.
    Set clear performance expectations, establish career development paths, and create meaningful growth opportunities for QA professionals at all levels.
    Provide training, mentorship, and guidance to engineering teams on testing best practices — raising the quality bar across the entire engineering organization.
    Develop and deliver scalable QA training programs and documentation that enable team independence and consistent quality standards.
    Foster deep collaboration between QA and engineering teams, breaking down silos and building a shared commitment to quality as a competitive advantage.
    Maintain regular and reliable attendance, including being present, on time, and prepared for work as scheduled.
    Performs other related duties as assigned.


Qualifications

EXPERIENCE AND EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:

    Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field preferred.
    7+ years of experience in quality assurance, with at least 3 years in a senior leadership or management role overseeing multiple teams or programs.
    Demonstrated experience driving end-to-end QA strategy across large-scale, multi-system platforms or complex enterprise applications.
    Proven experience leading and coordinating offshore QA resources and managing distributed testing organizations.
    Background in healthcare technology, pharmaceutical systems, or similarly regulated industries strongly preferred.

MINIMUM SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE AND ABILITY REQUIREMENTS:

 Technical Expertise

    Deep expertise in end-to-end testing methodologies for web and mobile applications, including integration testing, regression testing, and user acceptance testing.
    Strong command of test automation frameworks and strategies, with a proven track record of implementing automation at scale (e.g., 40%+ reduction in regression cycles).
    Extensive experience testing complex integration scenarios involving multiple systems, APIs, microservices, and third-party vendors.
    Proficiency with test management tools (e.g., TestRail, Jira, Azure DevOps) and defect tracking systems.
    Hands-on experience establishing and maturing quality gates within CI/CD pipelines and automated deployment processes.
    Familiarity with API testing tools (Postman, REST Assured) and performance testing approaches.
    Solid understanding of cloud platforms (AWS, Azure) and modern software architecture patterns.

Leadership and Problem-Solving

    Demonstrated success leading high-performing QA organizations, driving cross-functional collaboration, and influencing engineering culture at scale.
    Ability to manage competing priorities, align multiple teams around shared quality goals, and deliver results under tight deadlines.
    Proven track record of driving accountability for defect resolution and maintaining high-quality production releases with significant user impact.
    Experience establishing and scaling quality standards, frameworks, and best practices across large engineering organizations.
    Strong analytical mindset with the ability to identify systemic quality risks early and implement proactive mitigation strategies.

Communication and Collaboration

    Exceptional communication skills with the ability to engage and influence both technical and executive stakeholders, including product owners, engineering leaders, and C-suite.
    Ability to translate complex quality issues into clear business impact narratives and actionable recommendations for leadership.
    Experience leading productive bug triage and quality reviews, driving efficient and accountable resolution of issues.
    Strong documentation skills to create comprehensive QA plans, test strategies, and process documentation at an organizational level.
    Collaborative, solutions-oriented mindset with a track record of building strong partnerships across product, engineering, and operations teams.
    Experience with regulatory compliance standards (e.g., HIPAA, PHI protection) in healthcare technology is highly valued.

Physical Demands

